<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-feugier-carrier-driven-canalization> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Feugier, Mochizuki & Iwasa (2005) & Scarpella et al. (2006) PIN1 efflux carrier allocation, intracellular pool conservation, and open dendritic trees vs closed reticulate venation loops (Arabidopsis thaliana (dicot leaf lamina and procambial venation network))",
        "Feugier, Mochizuki & Iwasa (2005) & Scarpella et al. (2006) PIN1 efflux carrier allocation, intracellular pool conservation, and open dendritic trees vs closed reticulate venation loops faithfully reproduces Arabidopsis thaliana (dicot leaf lamina and procambial venation network) morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/feugier-carrier-driven-canalization-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/feugier-carrier-driven-canalization-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/feugier-carrier-driven-canalization-3> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) 2005-feugier-carrier-driven-canalization.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Arabidopsis thaliana (dicot leaf lamina and procambial venation network) specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is the weight of evidence (MorphoEval 0.1.0 overall 93.0/100, audit 2026-10-19-carrier-driven-canalization-audit-v2) and the assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/8871db0/2005-feugier-carrier-driven-canalization.py> ;
    schema:about "Arabidopsis thaliana (dicot leaf lamina and procambial venation network)" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: 3D viscoelastic cell-wall mechanical expansion coupled to turgor-driven leaf blade growth",
        "reconstructed_in_script: 2D hexagonal leaf lamina lattice solver (14x14 ovate blade, 6 faces/cell) verifying pairwise intercellular auxin flux antisymmetry |J_{i->j} + J_{j->i}| = 0.0 and demonstrating the topological transition from Model A open dendritic venation trees (Betti-1 = 0 loops, 10 free vein endings, 0 bipolar bridge cells) to Model B + Scarpella epidermal convergence closed reticulate venation networks (Betti-1 = 16 loops, 16 bipolar PIN1 bridge cells), plus a k_1 = 0 (`gnom`/`pin1` exocytosis block) negative control (0 loops, 0.0 vein fraction)",
        "reconstructed_in_script: 6-face hexagonal intracellular PIN1 pool conservation and regime bifurcation solver verifying exact pool conservation (error 0.0 < 1e-15), winner-take-all single-face polarization under Model A p=2.0 (dominant face share 0.9978 vs ref 0.9960), bipolar co-polarization under Model B saturating Hill exocytosis (dominant face share 0.5221 vs ref 0.5180), and 6-regime Pearson r = 0.9999 (p = 3.0e-8, RMSE = 0.0065)",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Automated ridge + chromatic warmth segmentation of the cleared dicot leaf tip venation skeleton specimen (`leaf_tip_venation_loops_specimen.jpg`, CC BY-SA 4.0, 539x351 px) extracting vein density (0.3585), Betti-1 = 205 closed polygonal areole loops, mean areole area (99.06 px^2), and mean areole compactness (0.7749 +- 0.0191 SE)",
        "reported_in_source: Feugier, Mochizuki & Iwasa (2005) J. Theor. Biol. 236:313-325 hexagonal leaf lamina auxin S_i and directional PIN1 carrier P_ij ODEs with conserved total cellular carrier pool P_total = P_{i,cyt} + sum_{j=1}^6 P_ij, proving that conserved superlinear allocation Phi(J)=J^p (p > 1) forces winner-take-all single-face polarization and strictly open hierarchical dendritic venation trees (Betti-1 = 0), whereas nonlinear saturating allocation Phi(J)=J^n/(K^n+J^n) allows multi-face co-polarization and closed venation loops (Betti-1 > 0)",
        "reported_in_source: Scarpella, Marcos, Friml & Berleth (2006) Genes & Development 20:1015-1027 ProPIN1:PIN1-GFP imaging showing epidermal PIN1 convergence points and transient bipolar (double-headed) PIN1 cells bridging secondary strands into closed areole loops",
        "transfer_boundary: 2D hexagonal cellular leaf lamina lattice PIN1 carrier-flux dynamics and graph cycle-rank topology mapped to cleared dicot leaf venation skeleton" ;
    pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/8871db0/2005-feugier-carrier-driven-canalization.py; output: docs/media/carrier_driven_canalization_comparison.png; organism: Arabidopsis thaliana (dicot leaf lamina and procambial venation network); checkpoint commit: https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/commit/8871db0; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.4.2, scipy 1.17.0, matplotlib 3.10.8, Pillow 12.1.1; spec_fingerprint: 2ca741f07ba825a876d0c45589ff7d455ac853c85ef60af0feb96546555dd50c; artifact_sha256: 60cbe1252bda975adf8955499006240bf329d5e1894f7dab81e6ae0ca89aa749; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/carrier_driven_canalization/carrier_driven_canalization_reference.json=d1b984c1cb7883c5..., datasets/carrier_driven_canalization/leaf_tip_venation_loops_specimen.jpg=e54c8add6cf7c916..., datasets/carrier_driven_canalization/paper_citations.bib=cb81009f386f3a51..., datasets/carrier_driven_canalization/scout_manifest.json=1de2b4f4c53ac234...}; supersedes_audit_id: 2026-10-19-carrier-driven-canalization-audit; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Feugier, Mochizuki & Iwasa (2005) J. Theor. Biol. 236:313-325 hexagonal leaf lamina auxin S_i and directional PIN1 carrier P_ij ODEs with conserved total cellular carrier pool P_total = P_{i,cyt} + sum_{j=1}^6 P_ij, proving that conserved superlinear allocation Phi(J)=J^p (p > 1) forces winner-take-all single-face polarization and strictly open hierarchical dendritic venation trees (Betti-1 = 0), whereas nonlinear saturating allocation Phi(J)=J^n/(K^n+J^n) allows multi-face co-polarization and closed venation loops (Betti-1 > 0) | Scarpella, Marcos, Friml & Berleth (2006) Genes & Development 20:1015-1027 ProPIN1:PIN1-GFP imaging showing epidermal PIN1 convergence points and transient bipolar (double-headed) PIN1 cells bridging secondary strands into closed areole loops; reconstructed_in_script: 6-face hexagonal intracellular PIN1 pool conservation and regime bifurcation solver verifying exact pool conservation (error 0.0 < 1e-15), winner-take-all single-face polarization under Model A p=2.0 (dominant face share 0.9978 vs ref 0.9960), bipolar co-polarization under Model B saturating Hill exocytosis (dominant face share 0.5221 vs ref 0.5180), and 6-regime Pearson r = 0.9999 (p = 3.0e-8, RMSE = 0.0065) | 2D hexagonal leaf lamina lattice solver (14x14 ovate blade, 6 faces/cell) verifying pairwise intercellular auxin flux antisymmetry |J_{i->j} + J_{j->i}| = 0.0 and demonstrating the topological transition from Model A open dendritic venation trees (Betti-1 = 0 loops, 10 free vein endings, 0 bipolar bridge cells) to Model B + Scarpella epidermal convergence closed reticulate venation networks (Betti-1 = 16 loops, 16 bipolar PIN1 bridge cells), plus a k_1 = 0 (`gnom`/`pin1` exocytosis block) negative control (0 loops, 0.0 vein fraction) | Automated ridge + chromatic warmth segmentation of the cleared dicot leaf tip venation skeleton specimen (`leaf_tip_venation_loops_specimen.jpg`, CC BY-SA 4.0, 539x351 px) extracting vein density (0.3585), Betti-1 = 205 closed polygonal areole loops, mean areole area (99.06 px^2), and mean areole compactness (0.7749 +- 0.0191 SE); transfer_boundary: 2D hexagonal cellular leaf lamina lattice PIN1 carrier-flux dynamics and graph cycle-rank topology mapped to cleared dicot leaf venation skeleton; does_not_claim: 3D viscoelastic cell-wall mechanical expansion coupled to turgor-driven leaf blade growth]" ;
    pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jtbi.2005.03.017>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1101/gad.1402406>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1365-313X.2005.02581.x>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pcbi.1000207> ;
    pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-feugier-carrier-driven-canalization-code-traceability>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-feugier-carrier-driven-canalization-model-fidelity>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-feugier-carrier-driven-canalization-morphometric-validation>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-feugier-carrier-driven-canalization-overall>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-feugier-carrier-driven-canalization-parameter-expressivity>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-feugier-carrier-driven-canalization-repro-package>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-feugier-carrier-driven-canalization-source-traceability>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-feugier-carrier-driven-canalization-specimen-match> ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-carrier-driven-canalization-audit-v2-feugier-carrier-driven-canalization-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-carrier-driven-canalization-audit-v2-feugier-carrier-driven-canalization-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-carrier-driven-canalization-audit-v2-feugier-carrier-driven-canalization-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-carrier-driven-canalization-audit-v2-feugier-carrier-driven-canalization-4>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-carrier-driven-canalization-audit-v2-feugier-carrier-driven-canalization-5>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-carrier-driven-canalization-audit-v2-feugier-carrier-driven-canalization-6>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-carrier-driven-canalization-audit-v2-feugier-carrier-driven-canalization-7>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-carrier-driven-canalization-audit-v2-feugier-carrier-driven-canalization-8>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-carrier-driven-canalization-audit-v2-feugier-carrier-driven-canalization-9> ;
    pk:hypothesisType "PIN1 Efflux Carrier Allocation & Intracellular Pool Conservation on Hexagonal Leaf Lamina Lattices" ;
    pk:weightOfEvidence 9.3e-01 .

