<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-feugier-carrier-driven-canalization-code-traceability> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Feugier, Mochizuki & Iwasa (2005) & Scarpella et al. (2006) PIN1 efflux carrier allocation, intracellular pool conservation, and open dendritic trees vs closed reticulate venation loops — Code-to-model traceability: 92/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Module and function docstrings map every equation to Feugier, Mochizuki & Iwasa (2005) Eqs. 1-11 & Figs. 3-7, Scarpella et al. (2006) Figs. 3-5, and the 3 formal Lean 4 theorems in `morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_035_carrier_driven_canalization.lean` (L1-37, L104-625)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-code-traceability> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/code-traceability" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-feugier-carrier-driven-canalization-code-traceability-1> ;
    pk:hasScore 9.2e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-feugier-carrier-driven-canalization-model-fidelity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Feugier, Mochizuki & Iwasa (2005) & Scarpella et al. (2006) PIN1 efflux carrier allocation, intracellular pool conservation, and open dendritic trees vs closed reticulate venation loops — Model fidelity to source: 94/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Implements the 6-face hexagonal PIN1 pool conservation and allocation bifurcation solver (`verify_hexagonal_pool_conservation_and_face_competition`, L104-227) and the 2D hexagonal leaf lamina lattice venation solver (`build_hexagonal_leaf_lattice`, `_compute_venation_graph_topology`, `simulate_hexagonal_venation_models`, L230-625) comparing Feugier Model A open dendritic trees (Betti-1 = 0), Model B + Scarpella (2006) saturating Hill + epidermal convergence closed reticulate loops (Betti-1 = 16, 16 bipolar bridge cells), and the k_1 = 0 (`gnom`/`pin1` exocytosis block) ablation control, backed by 3 machine-checked Lean 4 theorems in `morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_035_carrier_driven_canalization.lean`." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-feugier-carrier-driven-canalization-model-fidelity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-feugier-carrier-driven-canalization-model-fidelity-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-feugier-carrier-driven-canalization-model-fidelity-3> ;
    pk:hasScore 9.4e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-feugier-carrier-driven-canalization-morphometric-validation> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Feugier, Mochizuki & Iwasa (2005) & Scarpella et al. (2006) PIN1 efflux carrier allocation, intracellular pool conservation, and open dendritic trees vs closed reticulate venation loops — Morphometric validation: 93/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "`measure_morphoeval()` (L705-820) computes 9 reference-anchored morphometric measurements with uncertainty, Pearson r, p-values, and negative control: hexagonal PIN1 pool conservation error 0.0 (ref 0.0), pairwise flux antisymmetry error 0.0 (ref 0.0), Model A p=2.0 dominant face share 0.9978 (ref 0.9960, p = 3.0e-8), Model B saturating Hill dominant face share 0.5221 (ref 0.5180), 6-regime allocation Pearson r = 0.9999 (RMSE = 0.0065), Model A open tree Betti-1 = 0 loops (ref 0, 10 free vein endings), Model B closed reticulate Betti-1 = 16 loops (ref 16, 16 bipolar bridge cells vs 0 loops in k_1 = 0 ablation), specimen closed areole Betti-1 = 205 loops (ref 205, vein density 0.3585), and specimen areole compactness 0.7749 +- 0.0191 SE (ref 0.7749)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/morphometric-validation" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-feugier-carrier-driven-canalization-measurement-allocation-regime-sweep-pearson-r>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-feugier-carrier-driven-canalization-measurement-hexagonal-pin1-pool-conservation-error>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-feugier-carrier-driven-canalization-measurement-model-a-open-tree-betti1-loops>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-feugier-carrier-driven-canalization-measurement-model-a-quadratic-dominant-face-share>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-feugier-carrier-driven-canalization-measurement-model-b-closed-reticulate-betti1-loops>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-feugier-carrier-driven-canalization-measurement-model-b-saturating-dominant-face-share>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-feugier-carrier-driven-canalization-measurement-pairwise-auxin-flux-antisymmetry-error>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-feugier-carrier-driven-canalization-measurement-specimen-areole-compactness-mean>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-feugier-carrier-driven-canalization-measurement-specimen-closed-areole-betti1-loops>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-feugier-carrier-driven-canalization-morphometric-validation-1> ;
    pk:hasScore 9.3e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-feugier-carrier-driven-canalization-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Feugier, Mochizuki & Iwasa (2005) & Scarpella et al. (2006) PIN1 efflux carrier allocation, intracellular pool conservation, and open dendritic trees vs closed reticulate venation loops — MorphoEval overall 93.0/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 2 (v2) evaluation of `2005-feugier-carrier-driven-canalization.py` (overall weighted score: 93.1/100, up from 54.6/100 in v1). The remediated script integrates Feugier, Mochizuki & Iwasa (2005) hexagonal cell-level auxin S_i and 6-face PIN1 efflux carrier P_ij dynamics with exact intracellular pool conservation (P_{i,cyt} + sum_{j=1}^6 P_{ij} = P_total, error 0.0) and pairwise flux antisymmetry (J_{i->j} + J_{j->i} = 0, error 0.0); sweeps 6 allocation regimes across p in [0.8, 2.0] and saturating Hill exocytosis (Pearson r = 0.9999, p = 3.0e-8); demonstrates the topological transition on a 2D hexagonal leaf lamina lattice between Model A open dendritic trees (Betti-1 = 0 loops) and Model B + Scarpella et al. (2006) closed reticulate venation networks (Betti-1 = 16 loops bridged by 16 bipolar PIN1 cells, vs 0 loops under k_1 = 0 `gnom`/`pin1` ablation); and segments the SHA-256-locked cleared dicot leaf tip venation skeleton (`leaf_tip_venation_loops_specimen.jpg`, Betti-1 = 205 closed areole loops, vein density 0.3585, mean areole compactness 0.7749 +- 0.0191 SE). Overall 93.0/100 (faithfulness 92.8, reproducibility 93.4); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 8871db0; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.4.2, scipy 1.17.0, matplotlib 3.10.8, Pillow 12.1.1. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 94, Morphological realism / specimen match 92, Parameter expressivity 92, Morphometric validation 93, Source and data traceability 95, Code-to-model traceability 92, Reproducibility package 93. Output judged: docs/media/carrier_driven_canalization_comparison.png: rendered output of 2005-feugier-carrier-driven-canalization.py at 8871db0, image/png, 1258625 B, 2310×1428 px, artifact_sha256 60cbe1252bda975adf8955499006240bf329d5e1894f7dab81e6ae0ca89aa749 (sha256 60cbe1252bda975adf8955499006240bf329d5e1894f7dab81e6ae0ca89aa749), spec_fingerprint 2ca741f07ba825a876d0c45589ff7d455ac853c85ef60af0feb96546555dd50c. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 2ca741f07ba825a876d0c45589ff7d455ac853c85ef60af0feb96546555dd50c; artifact_sha256: 60cbe1252bda975adf8955499006240bf329d5e1894f7dab81e6ae0ca89aa749; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/carrier_driven_canalization/carrier_driven_canalization_reference.json=d1b984c1cb7883c5..., datasets/carrier_driven_canalization/leaf_tip_venation_loops_specimen.jpg=e54c8add6cf7c916..., datasets/carrier_driven_canalization/paper_citations.bib=cb81009f386f3a51..., datasets/carrier_driven_canalization/scout_manifest.json=1de2b4f4c53ac234...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-19-carrier-driven-canalization-audit. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Feugier, Mochizuki & Iwasa (2005) J. Theor. Biol. 236:313-325 hexagonal leaf lamina auxin S_i and directional PIN1 carrier P_ij ODEs with conserved total cellular carrier pool P_total = P_{i,cyt} + sum_{j=1}^6 P_ij, proving that conserved superlinear allocation Phi(J)=J^p (p > 1) forces winner-take-all single-face polarization and strictly open hierarchical dendritic venation trees (Betti-1 = 0), whereas nonlinear saturating allocation Phi(J)=J^n/(K^n+J^n) allows multi-face co-polarization and closed venation loops (Betti-1 > 0) | Scarpella, Marcos, Friml & Berleth (2006) Genes & Development 20:1015-1027 ProPIN1:PIN1-GFP imaging showing epidermal PIN1 convergence points and transient bipolar (double-headed) PIN1 cells bridging secondary strands into closed areole loops; reconstructed_in_script: 6-face hexagonal intracellular PIN1 pool conservation and regime bifurcation solver verifying exact pool conservation (error 0.0 < 1e-15), winner-take-all single-face polarization under Model A p=2.0 (dominant face share 0.9978 vs ref 0.9960), bipolar co-polarization under Model B saturating Hill exocytosis (dominant face share 0.5221 vs ref 0.5180), and 6-regime Pearson r = 0.9999 (p = 3.0e-8, RMSE = 0.0065) | 2D hexagonal leaf lamina lattice solver (14x14 ovate blade, 6 faces/cell) verifying pairwise intercellular auxin flux antisymmetry |J_{i->j} + J_{j->i}| = 0.0 and demonstrating the topological transition from Model A open dendritic venation trees (Betti-1 = 0 loops, 10 free vein endings, 0 bipolar bridge cells) to Model B + Scarpella epidermal convergence closed reticulate venation networks (Betti-1 = 16 loops, 16 bipolar PIN1 bridge cells), plus a k_1 = 0 (`gnom`/`pin1` exocytosis block) negative control (0 loops, 0.0 vein fraction) | Automated ridge + chromatic warmth segmentation of the cleared dicot leaf tip venation skeleton specimen (`leaf_tip_venation_loops_specimen.jpg`, CC BY-SA 4.0, 539x351 px) extracting vein density (0.3585), Betti-1 = 205 closed polygonal areole loops, mean areole area (99.06 px^2), and mean areole compactness (0.7749 +- 0.0191 SE); transfer_boundary: 2D hexagonal cellular leaf lamina lattice PIN1 carrier-flux dynamics and graph cycle-rank topology mapped to cleared dicot leaf venation skeleton; does_not_claim: 3D viscoelastic cell-wall mechanical expansion coupled to turgor-driven leaf blade growth." ;
